        <span class="tag">Plumbing</span>
        <h3>How to Fix a Leaky Faucet</h3>
        <p class="meta">Tools needed: adjustable wrench, screwdriver, replacement washer or O-ring &middot; ~30 minutes</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Shut off the water supply valves under the sink.</li>
          <li>Remove the faucet handle to expose the cartridge or valve stem.</li>
          <li>Replace the worn washer or O-ring with a matching size from the kit.</li>
          <li>Reassemble and turn the water back on slowly, checking for drips.</li>
        </ol>
        <p><a href="catalog.html">Shop plumbing supplies &rarr;</a> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <a href="technicians.html#plumbing">Still leaking? Find a plumber &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="directory-item" id="hanging-heavy" style="display:block;">
        <span class="tag">Fasteners</span>
        <h3>How to Hang Something Heavy on Drywall</h3>
        <p class="meta">Tools needed: stud finder, drill, level &middot; ~20 minutes</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Use a stud finder to locate studs; hang directly into a stud when possible.</li>
          <li>If no stud is available, use a rated toggle bolt anchor for the item's weight.</li>
          <li>Mark and level your hanging points before drilling.</li>
          <li>Drill pilot holes, insert anchors, and mount your item.</li>
        </ol>
        <p><a href="catalog.html">Shop fasteners &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="directory-item" id="door-lock" style="display:block;">
        <span class="tag">Door Hardware</span>
        <h3>How to Fix a Door That Won't Lock</h3>
        <p class="meta">Tools needed: screwdriver, file (optional) &middot; ~15 minutes</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Close the door and check whether the latch aligns with the strike plate.</li>
          <li>If it's off by a small amount, file the strike plate opening slightly.</li>
          <li>If it's off by more, reposition or replace the strike plate.</li>
          <li>Tighten loose hinge screws, which are a common hidden cause of misalignment.</li>
        </ol>
        <p><a href="catalog.html">Shop door hardware &rarr;</a> &nbsp;|&nbsp; <a href="technicians.html#locksmith">Need a locksmith? &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="directory-item" id="outlet" style="display:block;">
        <span class="tag">Electrical</span>
        <h3>How to Safely Check a Dead Outlet</h3>
        <p class="meta">Tools needed: non-contact voltage tester &middot; ~10 minutes &middot; Safety first</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Check the breaker panel for a tripped breaker first.</li>
          <li>Use a non-contact voltage tester to confirm the outlet is not live before touching it.</li>
          <li>If the breaker is fine and the outlet still doesn't work, the issue is likely wiring — this is a job for a licensed electrician.</li>
        </ol>
        <p><a href="technicians.html#electrical">Find an electrician &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="directory-item" id="painting" style="display:block;">
        <span class="tag">Paint &amp; Supplies</span>
        <h3>How to Paint a Room Like a Pro</h3>
        <p class="meta">Tools needed: roller, brush, painter's tape, drop cloth &middot; ~1 day</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Clean walls and patch any holes; let patches dry fully.</li>
          <li>Tape off trim, outlets, and ceiling lines.</li>
          <li>Cut in edges with a brush, then roll large areas in a &quot;W&quot; pattern.</li>
          <li>Apply a second coat after the first has fully dried, usually 2-4 hours.</li>
        </ol>
        <p><a href="catalog.html">Shop paint &amp; supplies &rarr;</a></p>
